  (text "J802 GPS port: JST GH 6-pin, Pixhawk GPS pinout: 1 VCC, 2 TX (to GPS RX),\n3 RX (from GPS TX), 4 SCL, 5 SDA, 6 GND. 100R series on the UART (GPIO36 / GPIO32);\nSCL/SDA (GPS compass) share the board I2C bus. PPS (GPIO39) is the TP801 solder pad.\nR806 holds GPS_TXD high with no module (GPIO36 has no pull-up); R807 holds PPS low.\nGPS supply = 3V3 by default (JP801 1-2); cut 1-2 and bridge 2-3 for a 5 V module\n(Pixhawk GPS units), fused by F803 (200 mA). Qwiic J803 also takes u-blox I2C (0x42).\nSpare GPIOs on test pads: TP803 IO15, TP806 IO33, TP807 +3V3, TP808 GND.\nIO15 is a strapping pin: do not pull it low at boot."
    (at 147.32 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "69f07e31-3430-44b0-b0a9-f2f7010efeeb")
  )
  (text "INDICATOR LEDS: side-view Lite-On LTST-S270 (1.6 x 1.2 mm) on the\nright board edge, lighting out through the case wall.\nActive high: GPIO = 1 -> LED on, 2-4 mA through 330R.\nD801 P1 green (GPIO18), D802 P2 yellow (GPIO19): process.\nD803 USER blue (GPIO5): free for the program. GPIO5 is a strapping\npin (SDIO slave timing only, unused); it may flicker at boot."
    (at 25.4 177.8 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "7bab1f46-96e0-4f8e-be2e-7062097e394f")
  )
